@startuml review_activity_flow
title Lightweight engineering review activity flow

start
:Identify change type;
:State requirement or scenario;
:Name affected boundary\nAPI, domain service, data, upstream, docs;

if (Behavior already specified?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Add smallest validation check\nunit, API, schema, regression, or manual script;
endif

repeat
  :Make smallest correct change;
  :Run local validation;
  if (Validation failed?) then (yes)
    :Fix failing behavior;
  endif
repeat while (Validation failed?) is (yes) not (no)

:Inspect design impact\ncoupling, ownership, errors, data state;

if (Risk is external, irreversible,\nsecurity, reliability, or safety related?) then (yes)
  fork
    :Trace requirement to code and tests;
  fork again
    :Record residual risks and rollback/recovery;
  fork again
    :Check logs, metrics, and audit evidence;
  end fork
else (no)
  :Keep review note lightweight;
endif

:Update canonical docs only if behavior changed;
:Summarize requirement fit,\ndesign impact, validation,\nand residual risk;
stop

@enduml
